Accepted certificate contract:
- Claim identity is kind, authority, authority id, context, operation, subject,
  and classifier. A Claim does not select a preferred Derivation.
- A Derivation concludes one Claim and refers only to accepted premise Claim
  ids or explicit scoped premise tuples admitted by its rule.
- Every transparent term export records the exact accepted source Claim id.
- Every Universe constraint records its numerical edge and exact accepted
  source Claim/authority provenance. Equal numerical edges may coexist when
  their provenance differs.
- No reserved legacy assumption field is serialized.
